When I used this application source code  for checking code quality and vulnerabilities ckeck then SonarQube Server analyze the Error like "Coverage of New code is less then 80%" this simply meaning that "Jest" are not preform the src code before check at sonarQube analysis.

Fix this error:-
1. Verify the package.json file :- from the content of package.json file we can identifies the application dependencies and application fronted code in which code build.

like this application is build in "react=frontend", "node.js=backend"

Update 1:-

here we add one line inside the 
"script":{
"test:coverage": "react-scripts test --coverage --watchAll=false --passWithNoTests --ci",
}

here :-
--coverage; generate coverage/lcov.info
--watchAll=false; runs once (required for jenkins/CI)
--passWithNoTests; prevents CI failure if there are no test file yet
--ci; disable interactive prompts

Optional but recomended - add Jest coverage config so CSS/images are ignored (prevents low % from non-testable files):
"jest": {
  "collectCoverageFrom": [
    "src/**/*.{js,jsx}",
    "!src/index.js",
    "!src/reportWebVitals.js",
    "!src/**/*.test.{js,jsx}"
  ],
  "coveragePathIgnorePatterns": [
    "/node_modules/",
    "/src/Photos/"
  ]
}

place this at the top level of package.json (siblings of "scripts",not inside it).

